Getting started:

(1) Install Overture from the github repo:
    https://github.com/wdhenshaw/overtureFramework.git

(2) Clone a version of CgWave from github 

    git clone https://github.com/wdhenshaw/cgwave.git cgwave

(3) Define the CGWAVE enviromental variable, e.g.
    setenv CGWAVE /home/henshw/cgwave

(4) If you want to use PETSc (e.g. for WaveHoltz and EigenWave) build PETSc and set the 
    enironmental variable PETSC_DIR, for example,

    setenv PETSC_DIR /home/henshw/software/petsc

(5) If you want to compute eigenpairs (with EigenWave) you will need to build SLEPSc and then
    set the environmental variable SLEPSC_DIR, for example

    setenv SLEPSC_DIR /home/henshw/software/slepc

(6) Build CgWave. in the cgwave directory type:
    > make

  This will create the executable cgwave/bin/cgWave


(7) Run the regression tests:
   > make check 
 of 
   > make check-quiet

(8) Goto the cgwave/runs directory to see some sample command files. 

